    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrĕcūsābĭlis</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		2. inrecusabilis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not to be refused</i> (post class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occasio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 3, 1, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 60, 14</span></i>.
			—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrĕcūsābĭlĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>without possibility of refusal</i>, Rustic. c.
			Aceph. p. 1218.</div>
